{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787080569,"nonce":"riwoj7zaNoqr8zZe1yUP3IJfDcA=","title":"`resolvedAfter` answers a question about the whole group with one case's duration, and falls back to `FirstSeenAt` — the field `GroupView` says a card must never present as the start","message":"**What is wrong.** `resolvedAfter` (`internal/channels/render/slack/reply.go:469-477`) has exactly one caller: the `reasonAllResolved` arm at `:146-148`, which draws *\"All resolved after `\u003cd\u003e` — N of M instances\"*. That sentence is about the generation. The function answers it with `v.Case.Duration` whenever a focused case is present, and only otherwise measures the group. Both branches are wrong in a different way.\n\n**The demonstration.** The first branch: `if v.Case != nil \u0026\u0026 v.Case.Duration \u003e 0 { return humanDuration(v.Case.Duration) }`. `CaseView.Duration` is one episode's span (`internal/channels/domain/view.go:102-114`), and `all_resolved` is emitted when every member of the generation has stopped firing. On a group of ten pods that started failing over forty minutes, the card reports the duration of whichever case the view happened to focus — the last one to resolve, or the first, depending on how the notification was raised — as the duration of an outage the same sentence goes on to say involved ten instances. The number an operator reads as \"how long were we down\" is one member's.\n\nThe second branch: `if !v.Group.FirstSeenAt.IsZero() \u0026\u0026 v.Group.LastActivityAt.After(v.Group.FirstSeenAt) { return humanDuration(v.Group.LastActivityAt.Sub(v.Group.FirstSeenAt)) }`. `GroupView` carries both `StartedAt` and `FirstSeenAt` and its doc comment (`view.go:64-70`) exists to forbid exactly this substitution: *\"StartedAt is when the SIGNAL started, taken from upstream's own `startsAt`. FirstSeenAt is when OTO first heard about it. They are different facts and the card must not present the second as the first: the gap is oto's latency plus Alertmanager's `group_wait`, and it was twenty-one minutes in the first live run.\"* `GroupFacts.StartedAt()` on the notification side makes the same argument at greater length (`internal/notification/domain/snapshot.go:97-102`, `:135-140`) and exists so that *\"every renderer, the API and the UI answer the question the same way\"*. This renderer does not use it. Twenty-one minutes is the measured gap, on a duration sentence — so the fallback under-reports an outage by the whole of oto's ingest latency.\n\nThe rest of the file already knows. `unackedFor` (`:479-488`) prefers `v.Case.StartedAt` and falls back to the group, and that is correct for its question — \"how long has nobody acknowledged this\" starts when oto knew. `resolvedAfter`'s question is the other one, and it inherited the same shape.\n\n**Why it matters.** \"Resolved after 4m\" is the single most quoted line oto produces: it lands in a channel, gets pasted into a postmortem, and becomes the outage duration of record. Both defects push it the same way — one member's episode is shorter than the generation's span, and `FirstSeenAt` is later than `StartedAt` — so the number is biased low in both branches, and low is the direction that makes an incident look smaller than it was.\n\n**Where.** `internal/channels/render/slack/reply.go:469-477` (`resolvedAfter`), `:143-152` (the `reasonAllResolved` arm and the \"N of M instances\" clause it sits in), `:479-488` (`unackedFor`, the correct shape for a different question) · `internal/channels/domain/view.go:64-70` (`GroupView.StartedAt` / `FirstSeenAt` and the prohibition), `:102-114` (`CaseView.Duration`, one episode) · `internal/notification/domain/snapshot.go:97-102` and `:135-140` (`FiringSince`, `GroupFacts.StartedAt()`, and why one function answers this for everyone) · `internal/channels/render/slack/testdata/reply_all_resolved.golden.json` (the rendered sentence).\n\n**Scope.** small.\n\n**Done when.** `resolvedAfter` measures the generation, not a member: it spans the group's start to the instant the last member resolved, and `v.Case.Duration` is not consulted for a sentence whose own next clause counts instances. The start it uses is `v.Group.StartedAt` — upstream's `startsAt` — with `FirstSeenAt` reached only as `GroupFacts.StartedAt()` reaches it, when there is no upstream start to have. `reply_all_resolved.golden.json` is re-cut if the number moves. A test builds a two-member group whose members started twenty minutes apart and asserts the sentence reports the span from the earlier upstream start, not the focused case and not oto's first sighting.","files":null}]}